{"parentUuid":"9d66649c-e547-44fa-8d36-ec55edae70c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZvGyYH7KhNQTUqKRti3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y8pU7ErTeJAnZN9EB22FjS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && grep -n -i \"short\" Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md | head; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold = \"  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles.\"\nnew = (\"  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. \"\n       \"`split.json`'s quarantine lists 1,201 flags, one per pool and held article, since 5 pool articles each reprint two held ones.\")\nassert s.count(old) == 1\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new))\np = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nreps = [\n(\"\"\"   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"   - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.\n   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.\n     - A seeded draw from those strata is screened by the tuned reader and by the teacher. Every article either calls a report is read by hand under `POLICY.md`.\n     - The credit check sizes it to find about 50 reports.\n     - Recall is reported per stratum and weighted. It's an upper bound, since reports both models miss go uncounted.\n\"\"\"),\n]\nfor old, new in reps:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"digits in the shingles\" Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","description":"Fix the quarantine wording and add the 2C plan notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8081,"cache_read_input_tokens":393444,"output_tokens":1336,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":320},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8081,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1336,"cache_read_input_tokens":393444,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8081},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y8pU7ErTeJAnZN9EB22FjS":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && grep -n -i \"short\" Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md | head; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold = \"  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles.\"\nnew = (\"  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. \"\n       \"`split.json`'s quarantine lists 1,201 flags, one per pool and held article, since 5 pool articles each reprint two held ones.\")\nassert s.count(old) == 1\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new))\np = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nreps = [\n(\"\"\"   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"   - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.\n   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.\n     - A seeded draw from those strata is screened by the tuned reader and by the teacher. Every article either calls a report is read by hand under `POLICY.md`.\n     - The credit check sizes it to find about 50 reports.\n     - Recall is reported per stratum and weighted. It's an upper bound, since reports both models miss go uncounted.\n\"\"\"),\n]\nfor old, new in reps:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"digits in the shingles\" Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","description":"Fix the quarantine wording and add the 2C plan notes"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"df37d46d-06a5-40ad-ae60-2c61dc000a76","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZvGxRoLejd5heGaRPKQ","requestRef":"b5266b89-8345-4a91-b766-06eabb532516","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb520020-6232-420f-9183-d574dd704ee0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:27:43.561Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"eb520020-6232-420f-9183-d574dd704ee0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"775e54ef-6487-4f79-8598-643421b87718","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8pU7ErTeJAnZN9EB22FjS","type":"tool_result","content":"132:   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\n146:    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\n152:    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f217fb90-c4cc-477d-baa8-70a3ee06d979","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:27:44.283Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"132:   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\n146:    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\n152:    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":119,"oldLines":11,"newStart":119,"newLines":16,"lines":[" 3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256."," 4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.","    - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.","+   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing."," 5. Baselines: a keyword rule, and base 4B both zero-shot and few-shot."," 6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded."," 7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.","    - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.","    - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.","+   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.","+     - A seeded draw from those strata is screened by the tuned reader and by the teacher. Every article either calls a report is read by hand under `POLICY.md`.","+     - The credit check sizes it to find about 50 reports.","+     - Recall is reported per stratum and weighted. It's an upper bound, since reports both models miss go uncounted."," 8. The failure log, and `eval/MODEL_CARD.md`."," 9. The local export and the offline proof."," 10. The full pass over all triaged candidates."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":831,"oldLines":7,"newStart":831,"newLines":7,"lines":["   - The rule flags all 603 one-story pairs of the randomly drawn strata. The lowest share is 0.105 (`dev-0088`) and the fewest shared runs is 6, so the rule sits just under both.","   - The large clusters' least similar pairs are the hardest by construction, and eval A's links group them anyway.","   - It flags 12 of the 17 randomly drawn pairs of two stories, since those pairs share passages. A false flag only keeps an article out of training.","-  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. Most are short repeated texts: mediums' cards and patent-medicine adverts re-run in later issues, steamer timetables, market columns, and wire passages two papers share. An advert of 50 words has about 40 seven-word runs, of which one in eight is kept, so a few OCR errors leave it without the two shared runs a link needs.","+  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. `split.json`'s quarantine lists 1,201 flags, one per pool and held article, since 5 pool articles each reprint two held ones. Most are short repeated texts: mediums' cards and patent-medicine adverts re-run in later issues, steamer timetables, market columns, and wire passages two papers share. An advert of 50 words has about 40 seven-word runs, of which one in eight is kept, so a few OCR errors leave it without the two shared runs a link needs."," - **The strata** (`scripts/gold_draw.py`, `eval/results/phase2c/gold_draw.json`). A candidate falls in the first that fits:","   1. **Three edge-case slices** the archive holds too few of to meet by chance (SRS 7.3), found by pattern: phantom ships, trains and lights (E8), hoaxes and pranksters (E6), and text not in English (E12). The other eleven slices are common among candidates, and 2C.2 counts each slice on the labels.","   2. **Before 1850:** 2.2% of candidates. A proportional share would be about 7 of 300, too few for B8's decade slices."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"df37d46d-06a5-40ad-ae60-2c61dc000a76","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb520020-6232-420f-9183-d574dd704ee0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
